# ── WORKER SCRATCH (founder convention: 2026-08-29) ──
# Autonomous loop workers (Hermes kanban) MUST dump all dirty/temp/throwaway
# artifacts here — NEVER in the repo root. Files here are gitignored so they
# can NEVER be committed, even by `git add -A`. If a worker needs a scratch
# file, it goes in scratch/ (or tmp/). Root-level _*.py / verify_*.sh are
# banned from the tracked tree.
scratch/
tmp/
_*.py
verify_*.sh
*.tmp
*_tmp.py

# Editor / tool backup files
*.new
*.bak
*.tmp
services/crawler/queue_data/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.venv/
build/

# ── THROWAWAY WORKER PROBES (founder convention: 2026-10-22) ──────────────
# 33 one-off probe/debug scripts and captured API-response dumps were found
# committed at the repo ROOT on 2026-10-22 (audit_check.py, check_amazon_*.py,
# repro_bug.py, verify_fix.py, .hc_tmp/*.json, jaipur_search.json, ...). They are
# never referenced by any tracked code or doc -- verified with `git grep -F` over
# the whole tree before removal.
#
# The pre-existing rules (`_*.py`, `verify_*.sh`, `scratch/`, `tmp/`) did NOT
# catch them because they were already TRACKED: .gitignore only affects untracked
# files. A rule that matches the actual names is what stops a re-commit.
#
# Root-level probe scripts (audit_*, check_*, repro_*, verify_*, inspect_*,
# fix_indent, round_results, tmp_repro) -- never commit these.
/audit_*.py
/check_*.py
/repro_*.py
/verify_*.py
/inspect_*.py
/fix_indent.py
/round_results.py
/tmp_repro.py
/test_ci_failures.py
/test_neg_live.py
/test_schema_live.py

# Captured API-response dumps (one-off curl/urllib output, not fixtures).
/.hc_tmp/
/jaipur_search.json

# Stale dated audit reports -- the live report is AUDIT_REPORT.md.
/AUDIT_REPORT_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9].md
